aiproducthub-cn-499196.en:
Make me a video. The topic is: Is relativity real? Length over 2 minutes, landscape 1080P; my requirement is: you can use any tools and techniques you think are suitable, and make the best, most stunning result.
Do an independent review before delivery to make sure the quality, content and motion effects make it a viral-hit-level video.

Topic: Is relativity real?

I'm putting relativity "on trial." There are now six witnesses, so let's see whether what relativity says is actually true or false:

Mercury's orbital precession, drawing a "flower";

The 1919 total solar eclipse, the bend in spacetime where starlight is bent by the Sun;

The "muon rain" falling from 15 km up;

Atomic clocks flown around the Earth, and your head aging faster than your feet;

The GPS satellite clocks' +45 −7 = +38 microseconds;

The spacetime ripples and gravitational-wave waveform from merging black holes, and finally the black hole photo.

copperforgeai-365603.en:
Work from the last 2 days: a fully procedural vertical machining center;
Everything is made with three.js, and this feels comparable in quality to what I used to get from modeling tools like tripo3D;

A vertical machining center is the most common kind of machine tool in a machine shop: the workpiece is clamped on the table, the spindle points straight down and spins the tool to cut; the tool magazine holds a ring of tools, and when one is needed, the tool-change arm swaps it with the one in the spindle at the same time. This web page turns a vertical machining center into a 3D explainer you can rotate, section and take apart, and it works in portrait on a phone. The model JX-850 is fictional; with real drawings it could be made more realistic and accurate.

Small and medium businesses can drop the brochure and introduce their equipment to customers with precise web pages and videos like this.
The main point is that it is cheap and fast. I plan to gradually build some core equipment of the machinery industry. This was made with opus5.5+three.js.

Live interactive link: https://amn8n.com/works/jx850/overview/
